B5 mutation check, 2026-11-10 06:46 UTC
Each mutant injects one bug into a copy of the repository. Mutants of resv_ctrl and sched_pkg run U10 first; then
tb_mesh_b (4x4, design B) is rebuilt and BP06, BP03, BP07, BP01, BP04, BP09, BP05 +QUICK and BP10 +QUICK run at
seed 1, in that order, until one fails. Every RTL $fatal is turned into $display, so the RTL assertions report but
cannot stop the run: only the testbench (U10's model, router_checker, ni_checker, sinks, scoreboard, idle checks) can
kill a mutant. A survivor is run again with the assertions on.
Killed = a run fails (RESULT FAIL, $fatal, hang, or no RESULT line); the reason is the first error.
An earlier run without U10 (stopped after C01) showed the mesh tests alone miss C01, the threshold one flit off:
they never decide at exactly fill + res + B_MAX = SPACE; U10 catches it in its first cycle (the smallest space).

